/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 114 0 R
/T (The nonce k must never be reused across two signatures with the same private key. Reuse allows an adversary to recover the private key d with simple algebra -- a well-known vulnerability in naive ECDSA implementations. TagWraps uses os.urandom\(\) in Python, which delegates to the operating system CSPRNG. This is the same mechanism used by OpenSSL and the majority of TLS libraries.)
/E (The nonce k must never be reused across two signatures with the same private key. Reuse allows an adversary to recover the private key d with simple algebra -- a well-known vulnerability in naive ECDSA implementations. TagWraps uses os.urandom\(\) in Python, which delegates to the operating system CSPRNG. This is the same mechanism used by OpenSSL and the majority of TLS libraries.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [38]
>>
