/T (Once specific bits in these lock bytes are set to 1, the corresponding memory pages become permanently read-only. This is enforced in hardware by the chip's internal state machine and cannot be reversed by any software command. Even a device with full NFC read/write capability cannot overwrite a locked page. The lock is permanent and survives chip resets, power cycles, and electromagnetic interference.)
